        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mia Hansen-Løve, Isabelle Huppert, Lola Créton\n- Films: Things to Come, Goodbye First Love, Something in the Air\n- Events: 66th Berlin International Film Festival\n- Awards: Silver Bear for Best Director\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, Goodbye First Love was released as a Franco-German film directed by Mia Hansen-Løve.\n- In 2011, Lola Créton had a lead role in Goodbye First Love.\n- In 2012, Lola Créton had a lead role in Something in the Air.\n- In 2016, Mia Hansen-Løve won the Silver Bear for Best Director for Things to Come at the 66th Berlin International Film Festival.\n- In 2016, Things to Come starred Isabelle Huppert as middle-aged philosophy professor Nathalie Chazeaux, whose life is marked by a series of separations.",
